  "final_answer_preview": "According to Section 18 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, nothing is an offence if it is done by accident or misfortune, without any criminal intention or knowledge, while performing a lawful act in a lawful manner and with proper care and caution. This means that if harm occurs accidentally during a lawful act, it is excusable and not an offence, provided there was no negligence involved. Additionally, Section 19 states that an act done with the knowledge that it is likely to cause harm is not an offence if it is done without criminal intent and in good faith to prevent other harm. Therefore, if the act was lawful and performed with due care, it would not constitute an offence.",
